Section: 5 Related Work
Text: Another approach, known as knowledge distillation, uses the large model (the teacher) to generate soft training labels for the smaller student network (Bucilu et al., 2006; Hin- ton et al., 2014). The student network is trained by minimizing the cross-entropy to the teacher. This idea has been applied to sequence modelling tasks such as machine translation and speech recogni- tion (Wong and Gales, 2016; Kim and Rush, 2016; Freitag et al., 2017).

